{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Can a man be of profit to El</b> — like <b>והוכח בדבר לא יסכון</b> (proving a matter is of no profit). Some say: it means \"lean on,\" and its sense is that a man leans in his deeds upon the Place [= God], or a discerning man leans upon the Place and upon a man, only according to his deeds. The closer interpretation is that it is like יוכיח. Close to it is הסכן נא עמו ושלם. The sense is: will El rebuke a man, or will He rebuke between the two of them a discerning man."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:22.163022116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}